## B. Seamless infinite looping

This is one of the most important requirements.

The default background music should support continuous looping for as long as the application remains open.

Use the browser's appropriate native audio capabilities, such as an HTMLAudioElement with looping enabled, or an equivalent reliable audio playback implementation.

Requirements:

- Enable looping for tracks that are intended to repeat.
- Avoid gaps or silence between repetitions wherever technically possible.
- Prevent sudden jumps in perceived volume.
- Prevent abrupt cuts at loop boundaries.
- Do not repeatedly create new audio elements to restart playback.
- Do not repeatedly reload the same file at the end of each loop.
- Avoid adding multiple overlapping copies of the same track.
- Preserve the current playback state when the user opens and closes settings.
- Handle the end of the track reliably.
- Ensure that the music does not stop merely because an AI response starts or finishes.
- Support continuous playback for long sessions.

A crucial technical requirement: the loop point in the actual audio file must be suitable for looping. Simply setting loop=true cannot eliminate an audible discontinuity inside a poorly edited source file.

If an audio asset has an audible beginning or ending, do not claim that looping it automatically creates a seamless loop.

Where necessary and technically supported, implement a short configurable crossfade or another appropriate gap-reduction technique. Avoid crossfading two copies of the same audio in a way that causes excessive volume or phase problems.

For ordinary music files, use the browser's native looping capability as the default reliable solution.

If you cannot guarantee a perfectly seamless loop because of the source audio, explain the limitation in the UI or documentation without blocking the feature.

## C. Calm volume by default

Set a conservative default background volume, approximately 15–20% of the available volume range.

The music must remain subtle and should not compete with the AI conversation.

Implement smooth volume transitions when the user changes the volume or mutes the music.

Avoid sudden loud playback.

Do not automatically normalize the volume by increasing it to maximum.

Remember that browser volume control and source-file loudness are different things, so use sensible default values.

